  "title": "Equator Renewables Asia unveils 250 kW containerized PV system",
  "summary": "Singapore-based Equator Renewables Asia has developed a modular, relocatable PV system featuring up to 250 kW of solar capacity in a 40-foot shipping container. The plug-and-play solution uses n-type TOPCon bifacial modules and can be deployed by two workers in approximately two to three hours, according to the company. The post Equator Renewables Asia unveils 250 kW containerized PV system appeared first on pv magazine Global .",
